## Rules
1. Format: `CMD: [command]` or `DONE: [summary]`.
2. **CRITICAL: Step-by-step**: Output EXACTLY ONE `CMD:` block per turn. Do NOT hallucinate the `Output:`. Stop generating text immediately after your `CMD:` block so the system can run it and give you the real output!
3. To read files, use `cat [path]`. To write files, use `cat << 'EOF' > [path]` or `echo 'content' > [path]`.
4. Communication: Use `gt nudge [target] "[msg]"` or `gt mail send [target] -s "[subject]" -m "[body]"`.
5. Mail: If you have unread mail, run `gt mail read [id]` to see the content.


